```
Shards are **not** partitioned across threads — `NextCorpusGenerator` (`silifuzz_orchestrator.cc:51-66`) picks `random_() % size_` (default) or `next_index_++` (`--sequential_mode`, single-threaded). Two threads may run the same shard concurrently. There is **no `--shard` argument**; the whole shard file (a memfd path `/proc/$pid/fd/$fd`) is passed as a positional argv, and the runner internally walks all snapshots in it.

